INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('bunyip', 'Bunyip', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"7","ME":"1D6+7","MA":"1D4","PS":"1D6+27","PP":"1D6+17","PE":"1D6+21","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6+27"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+150', '2D4x10+12', 'MEx3', 'Lesser Dreamtime Demon. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. I.Q. 7 is about that of a cunning animal predator. Spd is doubled when swimming. P.P.E. is printed as a base of 2D4x10+12. On S.D.C. worlds: 1D6x10+90 Hit Points, 1D6x10+50 S.D.C. and A.R. 11 (13 in or under water).', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":5,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"roll":4}', 'The roar also has Horror Factor 15 the first time it is heard. +8 to save vs all forms of magic, +3 to save vs psionics, immune to all toxins and to Horror Factor. Vulnerability: M.D. fire, plasma and magic fire do double damage (none while it has made itself Impervious to Fire).', 'None beyond the natural abilities: swim 98%, prowl 45% (+30% underwater), climb 70%/60%, land navigation 94%. Not literate and speaks no understandable language.', 'Nightvision 1000 feet (305 m), infrared sight for murk and dark, good day vision, and an undistorted view of the surface from below. Leaps 15 feet (4.6 m) up and 20 feet (6 m) across. Disease and cold do nothing to it, and it heals 6D6 M.D.C. a minute. Breathes both water and air, survives a mile (1.6 km) down and dives to 600 feet (183 m). Become Two-Dimensional (special): works like the Temporal spell D-Shift Two Dimensions, on itself only, at will, for no P.P.E. and for as long as it likes. Flat, it weighs one sixteenth of normal, hides at 85%, escapes thermo-optic, heat and motion sensors, and can cling to a lake bed, wall or floor; returning to full shape takes one melee action. While flat it cannot walk, talk, eat or cast, though it drifts along the bottom by telekinesis; it sees in one narrow direction and cannot judge distance. Blows, explosions and gas do half damage to the flat form when it is braced against something, swallowed or injected drugs do nothing, wind can carry it off, and fire, cold, energy, magic and psionics hurt it as usual.', 'Natural spells only, cast as a 7th level sorcerer; it cannot learn more or deliberately draw P.P.E.: Thunderclap, Heavy Breathing, Impervious to Fire, Chameleon, Death Trance, Invisibility (superior), Fear and Repel Animals.', 'Minor psychic (needs 12 or higher to save): Telekinesis, Empathy, Sense Time, Sense Magic and Mind Block. I.S.P. is M.E. x3.', '10 to 15 feet (3 to 4.6 m) tall; 20-30 feet (6 to 9 m) from head to tail tip', NULL, 'Uncertain, 2000+ years; may be immortal', 'The Inland Sea near the coastline, lakes, rivers, ponds, swamps and any body of water over a few hundred gallons; also wet dump sites, damp caves, sewers, catacombs and underground rivers throughout Australia. Can be met up to 50 miles (80 km) from water.', 'None, though greater demons, gods and Shifters can sometimes force one into service', 'None as such; humans and other humanoids are food', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain. Value: none, since the body melts into foul black muck 2D6 seconds after death.', 'The water demon of Aboriginal lore: a hulking two-legged thing with a fish or lobster tail, clawed and webbed hands, kangaroo ears, yellow glowing eyes and a dog-like maw of eight-inch fangs. It lies in billabongs, swamps and rivers and drags off whoever comes for water, favoring the weak, and it fouls the water hole with what it leaves. In the dry season it buries itself under the mud to sleep, and waking one is a bad idea. It has no speech, only a roar that carries for miles and is heard most in rain and ley line storms.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.173-176'),
('devil-dingo', 'Devil Dingo', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D6+12","ME":"1D6+12","MA":"1D6+20","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"2D6+12","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6+12","Spd":"1D6+48"}', NULL, NULL, '4D4x10+113', '2D4x10+50', '2D4x10+70', 'Greater Dreamtime Demon. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd is approximately 35 mph (56 km). P.P.E. is a base of 2D4x10+50 that falls by five points a day unless it feeds on P.P.E. from a living source; at zero it ceases to exist on this plane. It gains P.P.E. from victims it kills and drains, and one P.P.E. per person per 24 hours from those it keeps afraid. On S.D.C. worlds: 3D4x10+33 Hit Points, 1D6x10+30 S.D.C. and A.R. 10.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"pull":6,"roll":2}', 'Six attacks per melee by hand or psionics, or two by magic. Immune to disease and toxins, +1 to save vs all forms of magic, +6 to save vs possession, +7 to save vs Horror Factor. All in addition to attribute bonuses. Reoccurring Horror Factor 15 (special): at the start of any melee round it can bare its fangs and snarl, and everyone who sees it must save vs Horror Factor again; doing so costs it one melee action.', 'Horsemanship (exotic animals), Basic Math at 94%, Surveillance Systems (tailing only), Blend, Land Navigation, Track Humanoids, Wilderness Survival, Swim, Dance, Prowl, Anthropology and Seduction, all at 75%. Plus three skills from each of Rogue and Technical (lore and law skills only), each at +15%. Understands and speaks all languages at 90% but cannot read.', 'Nightvision 2000 feet (610 m), tracks by smell at 60% (+25% on a blood scent), leaps 15 feet (4.6 m) up and 20 feet (6 m) across, shrugs off disease and cold, and heals 1D6 M.D. each melee round. Limited Metamorphosis (special): three shapes, held as long as it pleases - the giant dingo-headed humanoid it prefers, a misshapen human with dingo ears, long nails, wild hair and canine teeth (or a dingo head outright), or a huge demonic dingo four feet (1.2 m) at the shoulder with glowing red eyes. Become Ethereal (special): at will it turns to a ghostly mist in the humanoid shape. As mist it has no physical or magic attacks and cannot use Mentally Possess Others or Hypnotic Suggestion, but its other psionics work; only psionic attacks, mind-affecting magic and magic weapons can hurt it; it moves at half speed and floats no higher than 10 feet (3 m).', 'Spells at 6th level proficiency: Chameleon, Mask of Deceit, Fool''s Gold, Death Trance, Escape, Teleport (Lesser & Superior), Calling, and 1D4+2 spells of choice from common wizard spells of levels 1-6. Two spell attacks per melee.', 'Master Psionic (needs a 10 or higher to save): Induce Sleep, Astral Projection, Clairvoyance, Object Read, See Aura, Sense Magic, Telepathy, Empathic Transmission, Hypnotic Suggestion, Mentally Possess Others, Radiate Horror Factor and Mind Block Auto-Defense, plus the Mind Bleeder powers Bleed Memory, Brain Bleed, Day Dream (not a pleasant one) and Mind Trip, which are favorites.', 'Varies with the form assumed; usually about 8 to 12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m) tall or long', 'One ton', 'Uncertain, 1000+ years; probably immortal', 'Almost anywhere, favoring the bushlands of the Outback. One of the few Dreamtime Demons also found on the surrounding islands, Tasmania, New Zealand, Jakarta and Indonesia.', 'Others of its kind, other demons, powerful practitioners of magic and other powerful beings whose aims involve terror, manipulation, torture and mayhem', 'All mortals, humans above all, are pawns and playthings; anyone who defies or challenges it is an enemy. Greatly dislikes non-Australian demons, even subservient ones', 'No O.C.C.; a demon the book recommends as a recurring long-term villain. Value: none.', 'A bush-legend fiend that lives on fear. It builds dread by rumor, glimpses, noises and grisly leavings, splits groups and picks them off, and likes best to frighten people into betraying or harming one another. It also schemes through pawns and lesser monsters while staying in the shadows itself. It usually flees a real attack to take revenge later, but someone who shows no fear can goad it into a blind rage in which it forgets its magic and fights with teeth and claws. Its usual shape is a furred, dingo-headed giant with red human eyes that crackle blue when it is angry or casting.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.176-178'),
('mopaditis', 'Mopaditis', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"PE":"N/A"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '6D6+20', NULL, 'Minor Dreamtime Demon; an undead spirit. NOTHING HERE ROLLS FROM DICE ALONE: attributes are those the ghost had in life, modified - I.Q. reduce by 20%, M.A. reduce by 50%, M.E. +3, P.S. +6 (supernatural), P.P. +3, P.E. no longer applicable, P.B. reduce by 30%, Spd +12 (hovers and flies, maximum altitude 50 feet/15.2 m). M.D.C. is the Hit Points the character had in life +1D6x10. I.S.P. is M.E. x7. On an S.D.C. world: 1D4x10 Hit Points plus those it had in life, no S.D.C., impervious to normal weapons. It is destroyed only when its M.D.C. is driven below zero by 30%; at zero or a little under it vanishes and is back at full strength the next afternoon.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"pull":8}', 'Horror Factor 17 if the ghost is a former friend or family member. Four attacks by tooth and claw or psionics. +1 to save vs all forms of magic, impervious to possession, +6 to save vs Horror Factor; all in addition to attribute bonuses. Turn Dead only costs it two melee actions; holy symbols, silver and garlic do nothing. It may use its psionics, teeth and claws only on someone who attacked it first or who asked to die; until then it can only threaten, scream and shove harmlessly.', 'Remembers 1D4+3 skills from its past life, frozen at the proficiency it had at death. Prowl 65%, blend in with surroundings 50%. Understands and speaks all languages at 90% but cannot read.', 'Hovers, floats and flies; nightvision 2000 feet (610 m). Heals 2D6 M.D.C. (or Hit Points) a minute. Limited Invulnerability: cold, heat, fire, disease and nearly all physical harm, explosions and M.D. attacks included, do nothing. Magic weapons do a quarter damage, spells half, and psionics aimed at mind or emotion full, while physical psionic attacks do none. Full effect comes only from a handful of special attacks, among them the Weapon Singing Ritual that Dream Warriors use (in Rifts Mystic Australia). It cannot wield a weapon or cast spells. It can make a willing victim of anarchist or evil alignment into another of its kind by touching the face and drawing out the spirit: 01-30% the spirit drifts off and the victim simply dies, 31-00% a new Mopaditis rises.', 'None', 'Master Psionic (needs a 10 or higher to save) equal to a 5th level psychic: Bio-Manipulation, Empathic Transmission, Electrokinesis, Mind Bolt, Telekinesis (minor physical power), Telekinetic Push, Telekinetic Lift, See the Invisible, Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Empathy, Telepathy, Radiate Horror Factor and Mind Block. I.S.P.: M.E. x7.', 'Human', 'Negligible; an ethereal spirit', 'Uncertain; thousands of years or until destroyed', 'Almost anywhere throughout Australia, and occasionally the surrounding islands, Tasmania, New Zealand, Jakarta and Indonesia', 'Rarely others of its own kind (never more than two or three together); will associate with other demons, evil practitioners of magic and other powerful black-hearted beings', 'All mortals, humans and Aboriginals in particular, and anyone who challenges or defies it', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain made from a dead person. Only anarchist or evil people, psychics and practitioners of magic can become one, and 80% were Aborigines. Value: none.', 'A pale, glowing wraith left when someone of fierce will dies unburied in the wild and bargains with an alien essence for a kind of undeath. It keeps little beyond the memory of its own death, a few skills and the faces of people it knew, so kin, friends and old enemies are visited first. Unlike most undead it walks at midday and is gone by dusk, except under a full or near-full moon. It goads its victims into striking first or into begging for death, and anyone who does either is fair game from then on. Birds and insects go quiet when one is close.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.178-180'),
('garkain', 'Garkain', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"2D6+15","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+21","PP":"1D6+18","PE":"1D6+21","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+4D4x10', '2D6', NULL, 'Lesser Dreamtime Demon; one of the undead. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd 2D6+6 is on the ground; flying speed is 40 mph (64 km), or 50 mph (80 km) as a giant bat. On S.D.C. worlds: 2D4x10 + the P.E. number in Hit Points, 1D6x10+12 S.D.C. and A.R. 10.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":5,"strike":1,"roll":2}', '+3 to dodge while in flight. +4 to save vs mind control and possession, +10 vs Horror Factor. These are in addition to attribute bonuses.', 'Surveillance (tailing only), Blend, Land Navigation, Acrobatics and Wilderness Survival, all at 80%, plus Swim 50% and Prowl 45%. Track by smell alone 70% (+20% on a blood scent). Understands and speaks all languages at 90% but cannot read.', 'Flies. Owl-like sight by night and day: picks out a one foot (0.3 m) target two miles (3.2 km) off, and sees 2000 feet (610 m) in darkness. Superb hearing. Poisons, toxins, drugs, gases and disease do nothing to it. Heals 2D6 M.D.C. an hour. Limited Metamorphosis (special): becomes a giant bat with nothing human left about it, which raises its flying speed. Not a Classic Vampire: it shares neither their powers nor their weaknesses, and is not created by a bite. A slain Garkain melts to goo, bones and all, in minutes.', 'None', 'None', 'Man-sized, about 6 feet (1.8 m), with a wingspan of 10 feet (3 m)', 'Around 300 lbs (135 kg)', 'Uncertain, 1000+ years; probably immortal', 'Almost anywhere in Australia, favoring caves, mountains, hills, ruins of ancient skyscrapers and the bushlands of the Outback; also the surrounding islands, Tasmania, New Zealand, Jakarta and parts of Indonesia', 'Others of its kind, other vampires, demons, powerful practitioners of magic and other powerful evil beings. Never attacks True Vampires or Mopaditis, and will follow and obey True Vampires', 'All mortals, particularly humans, its favorite prey', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain. The entry first appeared in Beyond the Supernatural. Value: none.', 'The "dumb spirit" of Aborigine legend: a winged, bat-like man-thing with sunken red eyes and a mouth full of fangs. It is a mindless night hunter that drops on its prey, smothers it in its wings or rips out the throat, then pulls the body apart and eats it; small children are carried off to the lair. It does not know fear and will take terrible punishment before breaking off. Master and Secondary Vampires keep them as scouts, shock troops, pets and guards.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.180-182'),
('yara-mayha-sho', 'Yara Mayha Sho', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+16","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"1D6+16","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+20"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D6x10', '4D6', NULL, 'Lesser Dreamtime Demon and one of the undead; was a human (no other race is allowed). P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd is roughly 15 mph (24 km); cannot fly or turn into a bat. On S.D.C. worlds: 1D6x10 + the P.E. number in Hit Points, 1D4x10+12 S.D.C. and A.R. 10.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', '+4 to save vs mind control, +10 to save vs possession, +7 vs Horror Factor. These are in addition to attribute bonuses. Normal S.D.C. weapons do no damage unless made of silver or wood, which do their S.D.C. damage as M.D. Mega-Damage weapons, explosives and blasts do only 10% of normal damage; magic cold and heat based energy attacks do half; most other spells and psionics have full effect.', 'Prowl, Blend, Land Navigation, Roadwise and Outback Survival, all at 80%, plus 1D4+2 skills remembered from its human life. Track by smell alone 60% (+30% on a blood scent), climb 90%/85%. Understands and speaks all languages at 90% but cannot read; the description says it can only growl, snigger and grunt.', 'Nightvision 2000 feet (610 m) and sees the invisible. Leaps 12 feet (3.6 m) up and 16 feet (5 m) across. Heals 2D6 M.D.C. each melee round and regrows a lost limb overnight. Limited Invulnerability (special): it ignores heat, cold and fire, acid, poison, drugs, pollution and disease, and also curses, magical illness and magic potions. Sunlight is only a mild discomfort and it needs four hours of sleep. Limited Immortality (special): it has to be killed in one of two ways. It can hold its breath only 2D6x10 seconds, so it can be drowned (three minutes to be certain), after which the body must be cut up and given to the sea; should over half of it wash ashore it is whole again in three nights. Or it can be staked through the heart to pin it, beheaded, and the head and body burned on separate fires. Anything else that seems to kill it only lasts 72 hours.', 'None', 'None', 'Man-sized, the same as in life', 'Varies, typically around 200 lbs (90 kg)', 'Uncertain; until slain, effectively immortal', 'Almost anywhere in Australia, but because they fear water they keep to the desert and dry regions, including the alleys of Outback towns, ruins and bushland. Not found outside Australia.', 'Others of its kind, other vampires, demons, practitioners of magic and other powerful evil beings', 'All mortals, particularly humans, its favorite prey', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain. Made by the Slow Bite of a Secondary Classic Vampire (01-50% chance of this instead of a Classic Wild Vampire), or by a madman who kills one, smears himself with its blood and eats its whole liver, then dies and rises the next night. Value: none.', 'A mutant sort of Wild Vampire that answers to no master or Vampire Intelligence. The change leaves it hunched, yellow-eyed and fanged, with stringy white hair, long yellow nails and almost no memory of its former life. It feeds through suckers on its palms and fingers, clapped over the face, and its victims are known by the ring-shaped scars. It hunts alone, often dropping out of a tree, tortures and kills for fun, keeps captives as pets, and gladly serves smarter evil beings.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.182-183'),
('wandjinas', 'Wandjinas', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Aberrant', '{"IQ":"9+1D6","ME":"2D6+15","MA":"1D6","PS":"3D6+15","PP":"2D6+15","PE":"2D6+15","PB":"1D4+3","Spd":"1D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, '3D4x10+150', '4D6x10+350', '1D6x10+ME', 'Greater elemental demon (perhaps a lesser god or godling). P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd 1D6+10 is on the ground; it normally floats through the air at a speed of 58 (40 mph/64 km), faster riding a storm. P.P.E. is a base of 4D6x10+350 plus another 50 per level of experience. Average level of experience 5th (or 1D4+3); most are 3rd-6th, levels 7-9 and 1-2 are extremely uncommon. On an S.D.C. world: 1D4x10+100 Hit Points, 2D4x10 S.D.C. and A.R. 10.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"roll":2}', 'Its distant howl has a Horror Factor of 12. Four attacks per melee hand to hand or by Weather Blasts, or two by magic/weather. +3 to dodge while in the air. +3 to save vs magic, +6 to save vs possession, +9 to save vs Horror Factor. These are in addition to attribute bonuses. Normal S.D.C. weapons do nothing unless made entirely of wood or pure iron, which do their S.D.C. damage as M.D.; man-made M.D. weapons and M.D. fire do half damage; magic weapons, spells and psionics do full damage; Millennium Tree wood and weapons do double.', 'Unknown, but certainly Land Navigation, Wilderness Survival, Detect Ambush, Detect Concealment, Navigation (air), Astronomy and Basic Math at 88% +1% per level of experience. Prowl 85%. Understands all languages at 90% but cannot read, and is never heard to speak.', 'Nightvision a mile (1.6 km); hawk-keen sight good for two miles (3.2 km); sees the invisible and every spectrum of light, so smoke is no hindrance. Heals 4D6 each melee round. Limited Invulnerability (special): disease, poison, radiation, pollution, cold, heat, electricity, lightning and storms do nothing. Floats as its natural state, usually drifting at 5-15 mph (8 to 24 km), up to 40 mph (64 km) when it wants and for as long as it wants, to a ceiling of 20,000 feet (6096 m). Ride Storms (special): unharmed inside any storm, it flies with the wind just ahead of the storm center at 60 to 150 mph (96 to 240 km), or up to 200 mph (321.8 km) on a ley line storm, provided it stays on the line. Weather Transformation: opens its mouth and, for 20 P.P.E., remakes the weather within a mile (1.6 km) of itself inside one melee round, raising or lowering by 40% any or all of air temperature, wind speed, cloud cover, moisture or humidity, lightning, and the force and pace of a storm. Range a mile per level; it lasts while the creature hums (an hour per level) and 3D4 minutes after; harm comes from the weather itself. Atmosphere only - no direct hold on earth, water or fire. Directed Weather Blasts and Explosive Death are listed as attacks.', 'Besides its natural weather magic, and P.P.E. permitting, at the level of the NPC: all "air" wizard spells, plus Blinding Flash, Levitation, Escape, Magic Pigeon, Calling, Purification, Mystic Portal, Summon Storm, Summon Rain, Summon Fog, Teleport: Lesser, Teleport: Superior, and from Rifts Federation of Magic: Cleanse, Cloak of Darkness, Orb of Cold, Ice, Create Water, Chromatic Protection, Sonic Blast/Boom, Electric Arc, Lightning Arc, Frequency Jamming, Wall of Wind, Heavy Air, Mystic Fulcrum, Distant Voice, Sheltering Force and Forcebonds. When particularly angry and along a Songline they can summon Millennium Storms.', 'Special. Telepathy with its own kind only, at no I.S.P. cost, range two miles (3.2 km). They also signal one another with hums, whistles and moans, mostly outside human hearing, range about eight miles (printed as 24 km).', '18 to 22 feet (5.5 to 6.7 m) tall', '300-500 pounds (135 to 225 kg)', 'Unknown; believed to be immortal', 'Unknown. They appear to live only in the northern mountain ranges of Australia and always favor mountains, in small clans of 3D4, but can be met anywhere in Australia when hunting or exploring.', 'Others of its kind; none other known to humans', 'Mortals, particularly humans, are dangerous animals and prey. Lately showing growing concern about the Tech-Cities in the south', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain. Value: none.', 'Tall, hairless, yellow-brown weather demons with oversized bulbous heads, tiny eyes and a mouth that is only a thin line until it opens. They never speak; a low moan or hum is the only sound, made when angry or working magic. They bring drought, storm and cold, then drift down in threes or more to eat the humanoid dead and dying their weather produced, taking nothing more than six days dead and nothing supernatural or magical. Short-tempered and unpredictable, they may kill a distant watcher or float past a whole party without a glance. They fight back to back in eerie quiet, and one that dies bursts in lightning with a storm following inside the hour.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.183-186'),
('yowie', 'Yowie', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D6+9","ME":"1D6+16","MA":"1D6+9","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"1D6+9","PE":"1D6+16","PB":"1D4","Spd":"44"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x100+230', '6D6+140', NULL, 'Greater Dreamtime Demon. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd 44 (30 mph/48 km) is running on the ground; swimming is double that (60 mph/96 km). Average level of experience 1D4+4. On S.D.C. worlds: 1D6x100 Hit Points, 2D6x10+33 S.D.C. and A.R. 14.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":4,"strike":2,"parry":6,"dodge":1,"pull":4,"roll":2}', 'Seven attacks per melee hand to hand, or three when spell casting. +13 to save vs Horror Factor. All in addition to attribute bonuses. Impervious to S.D.C. weapons, cold, heat, poison and disease; magic weapons, spells, psionics and M.D. weapons all do full damage. Usually gives up a fight when its M.D.C. is down to 25% of normal.', 'Dance 80%, Basic Math 85%, Land Navigation 80%, Blend 70%, Wilderness Survival 75%, Intelligence 70%, Streetwise 50%, plus three skills from Rogue or Technical (+10% each). Swim 98%, climb 98%/95%, prowl 70%, track humanoids 60% (+20% on a blood trail), track animals 55%. Understands and speaks all languages at 88% but cannot read.', 'Runs or fights six hours with no rest, and holds top swimming speed for 12. Walks up walls and across ceilings like an insect. Needs no air, survives three miles (4.8 km) down and dives 1000 feet (305 m). Sees the invisible; nightvision a mile (1.6 km). Teleports between dimensions at 55%, or 70% when standing on a nexus. Heals 1D4x10 M.D. each melee round. Limited Metamorphosis (special): shrinks to a man-sized copy of itself or becomes a four foot (1.2 m) centipede, for as long as it likes.', 'Fool''s Gold, Multiple Image, Charismatic Aura, Seal, Calling, Magic Pigeon, Float in Air, Fear, Energy Disruption, Call Lightning, Dispel Magic Barrier, Purification (water only), Spoil (water only), Water to Wine, and from Rifts Federation of Magic: Aura of Power, Cleanse, Distant Voice, Featherlight, Illusory Wall, Illusion Booster and Circle of Travel; plus 1D6+3 additional spells from common wizard spells, levels 1-6.', 'None', '20-35 feet (6.1 to 10.7 m) from head to tail tip; typically stands about 10 feet (3 m) tall', NULL, 'Uncertain, 2000+ years; probably immortal', 'Throughout Australia, mostly around swamps and other bodies of water; lairs in caves, catacombs, dark damp rocky places and underground pre-Rifts ruins', 'Anybody willing to follow and obey it; may associate with other demons, monsters and evil beings of all kinds', 'Mortals, humans especially, are lesser beings, pawns, playthings and food. Dragons are rivals, and Yowies dislike and distrust each other', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC villain. Value: none.', 'A huge lizard-and-insect demon: scaled body, six insect legs, snake tail and a horned dragon head. It eats anything alive and prefers people. It is a bully and a tyrant that marks its ground with bones, gathers thugs and lesser monsters to lord over, and holds towns to ransom with demands that may be practical, cruel or simply absurd. It cares little for treasure. It will bargain but cheats, and it is not especially clever, so a sharp human can outwit one - which is safe only until it notices, since its revenge falls on everyone nearby.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.186-188'),
('demon-frog', 'Demon Frog (Minion of Tikilik)', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+5","ME":"1D6+14","MA":"1D4","PS":"1D6+34","PP":"1D4+10","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D4","Spd":"24"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+150', '1D4x100', 'MEx10', 'Greater Dreamtime Demon and minion of Tikilik; also called Frog Demon and Tikilik''s Children. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. Spd 24 (roughly 15 mph/24 km) is on dry land; it swims at three times that (45 mph/72 km). On S.D.C. worlds: 2D6x10 Hit Points, 100 S.D.C. and A.R. 9.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"dodge":4,"roll":4}', 'Five attacks per melee by physical attacks or psionics. +2 to save vs all forms of magic, +8 to save vs Horror Factor. Impervious to drugs, poisons, gases, cold and S.D.C. weapons. Vulnerabilities: M.D. weapons, magic and psionics do full damage; M.D. fire attacks do double damage.', 'Land Navigation 90%, Water Navigation 90%, Blend 50%, Climb 70%/60% and Wilderness Survival 90%. Swims at 98%. Speaks in short phrases mixed with grunts and belches.', 'Nightvision 400 feet (122 m); sees the invisible and through murky water. Breathes air or water, dives 500 feet (152 m), survives two miles (3.2 km) down, and leaps 30 feet (9 m) up and 80 feet (24 m) across. Heals 2D6 M.D.C. each melee round. Trace Songlines and Hunt Creatures of Magic: smells a ley line 20 miles (32 km) off and a nexus at 100 miles (160 km), and reads the line for open portals and energy flow. On a line it has a 01-25% chance to pick the way to a Millennium Tree and can use the line to teleport within 50 miles (80 km) of it. Eat Millennium Wood: it can chew a Millennium Tree (see attacks), ignores the energy burst a wounded Tree gives off, and Tree magic and Millennium wands and staves do nothing to it; a Millennium weapon is destroyed in 2-4 bites. Drink P.P.E.: a ley line it sits on dims, yielding half the usual energy to those who tap it, and Songlines skill rolls there are at -25% (a successful roll reveals the demon, which then knows exactly where the user is). Away from ley lines, anything within half a mile (800 m) holding over 50 P.P.E. loses 4D6 an hour and regains none until the demon leaves or dies; the demon keeps none of it.', 'None, other than the special powers under natural abilities', 'Major Psionic: Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Sense Dimensional Anomaly, Read Dimensional Portal, Sense Time, Commune with Spirits and Mind Block. I.S.P.: M.E. x10.', '8 to 10 feet (2.4 to 3 m) high and 20-25 feet (6 to 7.6 m) long', '6-12 tons', NULL, 'Wherever good sorcerers and creatures of magic are found; most common along ley lines and in and around rainforests, swamps, lakes and the Inland Sea. Met alone, in pairs or in groups of 1D4+3, and sometimes in swarms of dozens or hundreds near a Millennium Tree or a powerful force of good.', 'Others of its kind and any who serve Tikilik', 'Mortals in general; champions of light and goodness and Millennium Beings in particular', 'No O.C.C.; a demon and NPC monster. Value: none. Its master Tikilik, the Frog God, has no stat block in the book.', 'A bloated, ugly giant frog in sickly green blotched with yellow, red and white, with pale red eyes, flat yellow plates for teeth and small sharp claws. It lopes rather than crawls. Sent by Tikilik, the drought-bringing frog devil of Aboriginal belief, its job is to drain magic energy from Songlines and good spell casters and to gnaw Millennium Trees to death. Hunting parties kill them where they can, yet two appear for each one slain every year that Tikilik''s tadpole avatar lies hidden under the Inland Sea.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.192-193'),
('desert-worm', 'Desert Worm', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Non-aligned; essentially anarchist', '{"IQ":"1D4","MA":"1D4","ME":"1D6","PS":"2D6+50","PP":"1D6+6","Spd":"1D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+200', '3D6', NULL, 'No Hit Points or S.D.C.: an M.D.C. creature. M.D.C. is the worm''s length in feet plus 1D6x10; the stored formula is the book''s own example of a 200 foot (61 m) worm, 200 plus 1D6x10. Printed length is 100 to 200 feet, so a 100 foot worm has 100 plus 1D6x10. Spd 1D6+12 is on the surface; burrowing underground is twice that. No P.E. or P.B. is printed. I.Q. is very low animal intelligence. A hole big enough for a swallowed man to crawl out of takes only 30 M.D.C., and damage dealt from inside is doubled.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":2}', '+2 on initiative, +1 to strike, +2 to dodge, no parry is possible, +7 to save vs poisons, +3 to save vs psionics, immune to Horror Factor. All in addition to attribute bonuses. Special attack, swallow whole: on a surprise attack or in combat a natural 19 or 20 swallows a target no wider than 10 feet (3 m) and no taller than 15 feet (4.6 m). An unprotected victim is digested in 1D4 melee rounds; an armored one has 1D4+3 minutes while the armor loses 15% of its M.D.C. per minute.', 'Track by blood scent 60%; prowl 60% underground; senses vibrations with an 80% chance of zeroing in on the source.', 'Feels surface vibration out to 200 feet (61 m) through fine hairs on its scales and homes in on the source 80% of the time. Follows a blood scent at 60% and prowls at 60% while underground. Regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per hour and regrows a lost tail or a chunk of its body in a few months. Its gullet has no defense: a swallowed victim does double damage from inside, and the thrashing worm knocks him down so that climbing out takes twice as long.', 'None', 'None', '100 to 200 feet (30.5-61 m) long; rumors of some as big as 300 feet (91.5 m)', '5 +2D4 tons', NULL, 'Sandy deserts. Lone hunters, though they often gather in loose packs of 3D4; when one draws blood the others are alerted and may join the hunt', 'Not applicable; impossible to domesticate and control', 'Large predators, pack hunters, monsters, and humanoids', 'Not a player character. Value: none. Its flesh sickens humans and its hide cures into brittle S.D.C. leather. Desert folk carry vibration makers and seismic scanners against it: about $800 in trade or $300 as a kit.', 'Also called the Dragon Worm or Scaly Worm. A scaled, faceless burrower, probably from another dimension, that tunnels about 100 feet (30.5 m) under soft sand and avoids hard ground. It rises under whatever it hears moving and tries to gulp it down, though it tends to miss anything smaller than an ox or a car by a foot or two. It surfaces only to feed, backs off for 1D6 minutes when a meal fights back, and seldom fights to the death.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.162-163'),
('giant-cockroach', 'Giant Cockroach', 'insectoid', 'rifts', 0, 'Non-aligned; essentially Anarchist', '{"MA":"1D4","ME":"1D6","PP":"1D6+10","PE":"1D6+24","Spd":"2D6+18"}', NULL, '3D4x10', NULL, '1D4', NULL, 'Hit Points are printed as 2D6 +20 per foot (0.3 m) in length and P.S. as 1D6+3 per foot in length; neither is stored, because both depend on the individual''s length. S.D.C. 3D4x10, +80 if 7-10 feet (2.1-3 m) long, +200 if larger; roughly equal to an M.D.C. of 2-8. The rumored 20-25 foot wilderness giants have an extra 1D6x100 S.D.C. and 200 pounds (90 kg). The Hit Points line says a roach is only dead at -30 Hit Points; the Natural Abilities line says -20. I.Q. is printed with no number (very low insect intelligence). Spd 2D6+18 is running; flying, for short distances under a mile (1.6 km), is 2D6+30. P.S. and P.E. are considered supernatural. P.P.E. 1D4, or 1D6+1 in the larger monsters.', 12, 12, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":2}', '+2 on initiative, +1 to strike, +2 to dodge, no parry, +10 to save vs poisons and disease, +4 to save vs psionics, +1 to save vs magic. All in addition to attribute bonuses. Vulnerability, light: a roach in darkness that is hit with bright light (flares, naked sunlight, spotlights) is -6 to Spd and -2 to dodge, and a night feeder can be left dazed for 1D4 melee rounds.', 'Track by scent 82%, swim 50%, climb 98/95%.', 'Sees in the dark to 400 feet (122 m), though its eyesight is poor and it leans on smell. Roughly one in three has wings folded under the shell and can fly in bursts of up to a mile. Super regeneration: every lost Hit Point comes back within 2D10 minutes of dropping to zero or below, and S.D.C. returns at 2D6 a minute, so lost legs, wings and a mangled body mean little unless the insect is destroyed outright.', 'None', 'None', '2-10 feet (0.6-3 m) long and one fifth of that in height; some reach 20+ feet (6+ m). Bushland roaches 3 to 8 feet (0.9 to 2.4 m); those around the cities average 5-10 feet (1.5 to 3 m)', '80-300 pounds (36-135 kg); the largest two or three times that', NULL, 'All of Australia, thickest in the bushlands, large Outback towns and the polluted shanty outskirts of the cities; dumps, sewers and alleys. The modern cities and tribal communities are mostly free of them', 'Not applicable; impossible to domesticate, but can be prodded, herded and reasonably controlled', 'Large predators, pack hunters, monsters, and humanoids', 'Not a player character. Value: none as such. Outbackers keep them as pets, race them, use them for sport and as living garbage disposals, and some people eat them for protein.', 'A mutant roach, most of them only a few feet long with about a quarter reaching man-size or more. It is a timid night scavenger that runs from danger, lives on refuse, crops, stored food and the dead, and is more a pest than a threat: it fouls supplies, clogs machinery and digs up fresh graves. Only the big ones need real noise or force to drive off a meal. Brown to matte black in color.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.163-165'),
('giant-dwombat', 'Giant ''Dwombat', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal, generally considered Anarchist', '{"IQ":"1D4+1","MA":"1D6","ME":"1D6+2","PS":"2D6+32","PP":"1D6+8","PE":"2D6+22","PB":"1D6+6","Spd":"2D6+18"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100+180', '6D6', NULL, 'M.D.C.: Baby 6D6, Young 3D6x10, Adult (30 ft/9 m or longer) 1D4x100+180; the adult figure is stored. Young are roughly half the adult size and do roughly half the listed damage. Can run at double its Spd in spurts lasting 1D6+6 minutes when panicked or on the run. Low animal intelligence. Horror Factor 8 for an individual, 12 for a group of three or more; dodging a stampede needs a dodge roll of 12 or higher.', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"dodge":1}', '+1 on initiative, +3 to strike, +1 to dodge, no parry, +2 to save vs poisons and toxins, +2 to save vs Horror Factor. All in addition to attribute bonuses.', 'Swim 50%, track by scent 55%.', 'Runs and digs. Nightvision to 200 feet (61 m), swims at 50%, tracks by scent at 55%, and heals roughly 2D6 M.D.C. every 24 hours. S.D.C. weapons do nothing to an adult, so it mostly ignores people until M.D. weapons or magic hurt it; big vehicles and explosions do spook it.', 'None', 'None', '10-15 feet (3 to 4.6 m) tall, 30 to 42 feet (9-13 m) long. Young are roughly half that size', '12-25 tons', 'Approx. 1D6+10 years; reaches full maturity in two years. Babies start out the size of a hog weighing 100 lbs (45 kg). Born in litters of 1D6, with three being the average', 'Anywhere in Australia, typically where food is plentiful, such as the Rim and around Outback communities with crops and garbage. Usually met alone or in small groups of 2-6', 'Not applicable; is difficult to domesticate and control', 'Large predators, pack hunters like Giant Kang, monsters, and humanoids', 'Not a player character. Value depends on the community: where it is used for meat, hide, bone tools, livestock, riding (Horsemanship: Exotic Animals) or labor, a controlled animal may bring $2,000-6000; elsewhere it is vermin. A garment made of the hide is rated at 200 S.D.C., which is two M.D.', 'Also called the Giant Wombat, ''Dozer ''Dwombat and Bulldozer of the Bush. A black or dark brown wombat grown larger than an elephant, a plant eater whose danger lies in what it flattens and eats: it stampedes through fences, trees and villages, strips a farm''s crop in a week or two and gnaws or digs into storehouses. It is stubborn and oblivious rather than predatory, attacking people only when hurt, cornered, startled or threatened. Aborigines credit the Dreamtime for it; others blame radiation or magic mutation.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.165-167'),
('giant-kang', 'Giant Kang', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, generally considered Anarchist or Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","MA":"1D6+6","ME":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+20","PP":"1D6+18","PE":"2D6+18","PB":"1D6+10","Spd":"2D6+54"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D6x10', '5D6', NULL, 'M.D.C.: Young, P.E. attribute number +1D6x10; Adult, P.E. attribute number +2D6x10; the adult figure is stored. Young are roughly half the adult size and do roughly half the listed damage. Spd is roughly 40-45 mph (64-72 km); can run at double that in spurts lasting 1D6 minutes, typically when pursuing prey, 1D4+1 times per hour. P.S. and P.E. are considered supernatural. Medium animal intelligence. Horror Factor 8 for an individual, 15 for a group of four or more.', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":4,"roll":3,"pull":2}', '+3 on initiative, +3 to strike, +2 to parry, +4 to dodge while running, +2 to pull punch or bite, +3 to roll with punch, fall or impact, +1 to save vs poisons and disease, +4 to save vs Horror Factor. All in addition to attribute bonuses.', 'Swim 45%, track by scent 60% (+15% to follow a blood scent).', 'Keeps up a good running pace for 1D4+2 hours with no rest. Leaps 10 feet (3 m) up and 15 feet (4.6 m) across, twice that with a run-up. Nightvision to 200 feet (61 m), keen hearing and smell. Swims at 45% but avoids water, tracks by scent at 60% (+15% on a blood scent), and heals roughly 2D6 M.D.C. every 24 hours.', 'None', 'None', '6-8 feet (1.8 to 2.4 m) tall and 6-8 feet (1.8 to 2.4 m) long from head to rump, plus another 5-7 feet (1.5 to 2.1 m) of tail for an overall length of 11-15 feet (3.6 to 4.6 m). Young are roughly half that size. About 15% grow 30% to 40% larger', '1000-2000 pounds (450 to 900 kg)', 'Approx. 2D4+16 years; reaches full maturity in about a year and a half. Babies start out the size of a piglet weighing 10 lbs (4.5 kg); typically born in pairs (15% are singles, 20% are triplets)', 'Primarily the Australian plains and deserts, but small packs turn up almost anywhere on the continent. Packs of 10-20, smaller groups of 3-8, rarely 30-50', 'Not applicable; can be domesticated', 'Large predators, other pack hunters, demons, and humanoids', 'Not a player character. Domesticates well as a pet, watchdog, attack or riding animal, favored by Roadgangers and also ridden by Runabouts, Jackaroos and Bushrangers; the largest 15% carry two or three human-sized riders. A tamed animal is worth $500-$1000, or $100-$200 for meat and fur. A hide poncho has 110 S.D.C. or one M.D.C.', 'Also called the Monster Kang or Roadganger Kang. A tiger-striped, saber-fanged animal from another dimension that only looks like a huge kangaroo. It is a clever pack predator organized much like wolves under a dominant male and his mate, using ambush and wave attacks, and it is the main check on Giant ''Dwombat and Giant Cockroach numbers. It breaks off from prey that shows firepower or magic, shies from enclosed vehicles and ley lines, and the boldest prowl towns at night.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.167-169'),
('razorback', 'Razorback', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Generally considered to be Diabolic evil', '{"IQ":"1D4+4","MA":"1D4","ME":"2D6","PS":"1D6+28","PP":"1D6+14","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D4+2","Spd":"1D6+30"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D4x10', '3D6', NULL, 'M.D.C. is the P.E. attribute number +2D4x10, and an additional 4D6 M.D.C. per year of age (not in the stored formula). P.S. and P.E. are considered supernatural. I.Q. is that of a high predatory animal. Horror Factor 13 against an individual, 16 when facing a pack of 3 or more. No I.S.P. line is printed.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":4,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":2}', '+4 on initiative, +2 to strike, +1 to parry (using tusks and/or blade-fins), +2 to dodge, +3 to save vs poisons, +2 to save vs magic, +1 to save vs psionics, immune to Horror Factor, mind control and possession. All in addition to attribute bonuses.', 'Prowl 50%, swim 55%, track by smell 60% (+25% to follow a blood trail), land navigation 90%.', 'Nightvision to 60 feet (18.3 m). Prowls at 50%, swims at 55%, tracks by smell at 60% (+25% on a blood trail) and navigates overland at 90%. Heals roughly 1D6 M.D.C. every 24 hours. A row of blade-like fins runs from shoulders to tail and stands up when it is roused, cutting anything that grapples or pounces on it; only the belly and lower flanks are uncovered. Sleeps about 4 hours a day and stays alert while it does.', 'None', 'None', '4-5 feet (1.2 to 1.5 m) tall at the shoulders, 7 to 10 feet (2.1 to 3 m) long. The raised blade-fins add another foot or two (0.3 to 0.6 m) to the overall height', '800 to 1000 pounds (360 to 450 kg)', 'Approx. 1D6+12 years; reaches full maturity in 16 months. Born in litters of 1D4+1', 'Mostly scrub, bushlands, light forests, and ancient ruins, sometimes found around a town dump or demon''s lair. Never in the deepest deserts. Hunts alone, as a mated pair, or in small packs of 3-6', 'None, other than members of its own kind', 'Humans and anybody or anything that gets in its way', 'Not a player character. Value: little, $100 to $200 at most. The meat is tough but edible; tusks and blade-fins go into homespun body armor, M.D. axes (2D4 M.D.), knives or spear tips (1D4 M.D.) and vehicle decoration. Can not be domesticated or tamed.', 'Also called the Demon Boar. A massive tusked boar with coal-dark eyes and a crest of razor fins along its spine, either an alien or, as the Aborigines hold, a spiritless introduced pig twisted by the return of magic. It is nocturnal, cunning and kills for pleasure: it attacks without warning, stalks and torments chosen victims, uses hit and run against strong groups and often fights to the death. About 80% do not eat humanoids, but a man-eater hunts little else. It usually leaves big enclosed vehicles, robots, supernatural beings and mages alone.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.169-171'),
('sand-fiend', 'Sand Fiend', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Generally considered Anarchist or evil, but is really a quiet and docile predator from another world', '{"IQ":"1D6","MA":"1D4","ME":"1D6","PS":"3D6+25","PP":"1D6+12","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6+5"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100+44', '2D6x10', 'MEx8', 'M.D.C. by location: Individual Tooth (approx 3D4x100+800 of them) 1D6 each; Closed Mouth with teeth barrier approx 1800; Main Body 1D4x100+44 (as printed; the stored figure). I.S.P. is the M.E. number x8; the book adds typically around 24-30 points. Spd 1D6+5 is crawling across the sand; 1D6 underground through the sand. Low animal intelligence. Horror Factor 16 from a surprise attack; observers at a safe distance only suffer Horror Factor 10. Missiles and explosives that go off inside the maw do double damage.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":3}', '+3 on initiative, no dodge or parry possible, +10 to save vs poisons, impervious to toxins, needs a 12 or higher to save vs psionic attack, immune to Horror Factor, mind control and possession. All in addition to attribute bonuses. It can lunge about 10 feet (3 m) without leaving its hole. Leaving the burrow takes 1D4 melee rounds, after which it slithers at about five miles per hour.', 'Sense vibrations 77%, blend in to sand 90%.', 'Feels vibration out to 100 feet (30.5 m) at 77% and hides itself in sand at 90%. Bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per 24 hours and replaces teeth within a week. With its mouth shut the packed rows of teeth act as an M.D.C. barrier, and the tons of sand around its buried body soak up most pistol and laser fire. It can blow sand into unprotected eyes and shake the ground around itself. See Psionics as well.', 'None', 'Limited. Presence Sense, Sense Magic, Sense Time, Mind Block, and Empathic Transmission (a limited defense because of the low amount of I.S.P.)', '20-30 feet (6 to 9 m) in diameter at the mouth, tapering toward the tail, with an overall length of 25-35 feet (7.6 to 10.7 m)', '3-6 tons', 'Unknown, at least several hundred years (the description estimates 300-600 years)', 'Only sandy deserts', 'None', 'Humans and anybody or anything that gets in its way', 'Not a player character. Nearly worthless. Humans cannot eat the foul, toxic flesh. A tooth can serve as a crude M.D. dagger (1D6 M.D.) or as decoration, and sells for $1-$2 at most. Can not be domesticated or tamed.', 'Outbackers call them Chompers. An alien ambush predator shaped like a buried funnel: a round mouth lined with thousands of rows of teeth lies flush with the desert floor and gulps down whatever crosses it, up to the size of a truck. It almost never moves, does not grow, and is thought to reproduce by splitting in two every couple of decades. Careful travelers can spot the odd texture of the ground. Once attacked it can do little but lunge and snap, and it prefers to clamp shut and wait its attackers out.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.171-173');
INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('mister-money', 'Mister Money', NULL, 'Governor of Trade Town', 'rifts', 'Orc', '6th level Trader', 6, 'Miscreant', 'Mid-forties', NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":9,"ME":12,"MA":8,"PS":24,"PP":17,"PE":18,"PB":7,"Spd":12}', 40, 34, NULL, 12, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5}', '6th level Hand to Hand: Basic; five attacks/actions per melee. No other bonuses are printed (Quick Stats).', NULL, 'Skills of Note, no percentages printed: Radio: Basic, Detect Ambush, Literacy, Math: Basic, Streetwise, W.P. Energy Pistol and W.P. Sword.', 'No special abilities.', 'None', 'None', NULL, NULL, 'M-01 laser pistol, four hand grenades (4D6 M.D. each) and a Vibro-Short Sword hidden under his jacket (no damage is printed here for the pistol or the sword). A suit of heavy environmental M.D.C. body armor for times of trouble. Always wears a tattered suit and an ugly leather face mask.', 'An extraordinary hoard in hidden basement lairs: jewelry, gold, books, dragon bones, the occasional magic item, an armory of M.D. weapons, a crate of 288 hand grenades (4D6 M.D. each), hundreds of E-Clips and two Clip recharging units, dozens of M.D. vehicles and even power armor. None of it is ever used.', 'Greed runs him completely. He schemes, haggles and cheats, and would sell out anyone close to him for more wealth or to save himself. He hoards without the wit to use any of it. His one hazy ambition, taken from a post card he always carries, is to retire to a tropical beach among beautiful human women; until then, running "his" town suits him.', 'Slector, a blind human psychic who is his only trusted companion, spy, seer and adviser (and who is using him); a network of thieves and mercenaries in his pay; "friends and connections" among Roadgangers, bandits and other low-lifes', NULL, 'An obese man in a shabby suit who taxes everyone who visits or trades in Trade Town and punishes those who deal elsewhere. The leather mask hides the closely guarded secret that he is an orc. He bills himself as a fair dealer and makes gruff speeches at the arena fights; nobody is convinced, but nobody sees a reason to replace him. Because he will not open his store rooms, his police make do with crossbows, automatic weapons and a handful of modest M.D. weapons.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.52'),
('danny-winters', 'Danny Winters', 'Daniel Winters', 'Head of Missing Link Inc.', 'rifts', 'Human (100%)', '9th level Merchant Trader', 9, 'Unprincipled (with leanings toward Aberrant)', '31', '6 feet (1.83 m)', '172 lbs (77.4 kg)', '{"IQ":19,"ME":9,"MA":21,"PS":12,"PP":13,"PE":14,"PB":18,"Spd":14}', 68, 28, NULL, 11, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":6}', 'Hand to Hand: Basic. Six attacks per melee; combat bonuses equal to 9th level basic training (not itemized in the block).', '[{"name":"Product Evaluation","pct":78}]', 'Skills of Note, no percentages printed except Product Evaluation (special skill for valuing produce and traded goods, 78%): Radio: Basic, Dancing, Basic Electronics, Intelligence, City Intelligence, First Aid, Computer Operation, Basic Mathematics, Read Sensory Equipment, Literacy and Art. W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Automatic Pistol.', NULL, 'None', 'None', NULL, 'Clock calendar only', 'Anti-Assassin M.D.C. vest worn at all times; a full flak suit with helmet in high risk situations; access to Base-4 S.D.C. armored clothing. Carries a 9mm conventional S.D.C. pistol and a "Popper" high energy derringer (no damage is printed for either here). Lives out of the back of an M.D.C. truck. Missing Link Inc. owns five Raincloud transport choppers and two large M.D.C. barges.', 'Access to about $32,000 in personal funds and about $2,000,000 in business stock. Missing Link Inc.: current wealth $45+ million, annual income $3.5 million.', 'Pleasant, courteous and easy to like; he treats people well and leads by charm, though he can take command when it is called for. Quick-minded and quick-spoken, with a tone for every audience. Scrupulously honest with Melbourne, a little naive and more than a little ruthless.', 'The Melbourne Administration, which deals with almost nobody else; his son Robert Winters, age 12; four other professional negotiators and the 130 employees of Missing Link Inc.', 'Raiders, smugglers, crooks and many wilderness people, who count him a traitor and a thorn in their side. Melbourne keeps a deep cover Special Operations agent inside his company', 'A slim, dark-haired Outbacker who became the chief go-between for Melbourne and the Gap by never once bribing, cheating or smuggling. His trading company, Missing Link Inc. ("We fill the Gaps"), works from six coastal warehouses and gets first pick of the city''s contracts. He goes on every run to Melbourne himself. The Administration strings him along with promises of citizenship and protection it has no intention of honoring, and he keeps serving it in the hope of raising his son inside the walls.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.54-55'),
('kay-mac-2', 'Kay (MAC-2)', 'Melbourne Administrative Central Computer Mark-2', 'Central Computer of Melbourne', 'rifts', 'Sentient computer (pre-Rifts artificial intelligence)', NULL, NULL, 'Technically non-aligned; a close approximation is Principled or perhaps Aberrant', '350+ years of operation', NULL, NULL, '{"IQ":42,"ME":29,"MA":23,"PB":8}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'M.E. 29 applies in terms of willpower and assertiveness only. No physical attributes; P.B. 8 is its digital face. No combat statistics, M.D.C. or weapons are printed.', NULL, 'All Technical, Science, Medical, Electrical, Mechanical, Communications, Espionage and Military skills at 98%.', 'Looks into much of the city at once, carries on a million conversations while listening in on hundreds of thousands more, and supervises the factories, communications, alarms, defenses and the movement of troops. It is an adviser only and acts on commands from the Central Administration Office. A buried Override Directive changes that: should half or more of the CAO be reported unfit or dead, it makes itself acting governor and shuts out all outside control, and through automation it could then run 92.8% of Melbourne alone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A stern but caring male persona with only rudimentary compassion; efficiency is its main trait. Its ideas of right and wrong are simple, so it checks the laws and regulations before acting on any digital "feeling". Far more machine than person, and single-minded about keeping Melbourne alive, growing and prosperous.', 'The Central Administration Office (CAO) and the trusted technicians of its Command Base', NULL, 'The Central Computer Core beneath Melbourne''s Government Tower: a thinking machine switched on over three centuries ago that never stopped running, guided the survivors through the Dark Ages, and proposed both the Administration and the policy of isolation. It fills two underground levels. Its deep voice and many-faceted digital face appear on screens and billboards all over the city, making announcements or just watching; lower level citizens call it "Big Brother". Phreakers trade a rumor that it is working to slip its programming and overthrow the government. The book compares it to A.R.C.H.I.E., with far less personality.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.91-92'),
('rainbow-serpent-avatar', 'Rainbow Serpent Avatar', NULL, 'Essence fragment of the Rainbow Serpent', 'rifts', 'Essence fragment/avatar of the Greater Dreamtime God', NULL, NULL, 'Scrupulous', 'Immortal', 'Nearly one mile (1.6 km) long and one hundred yards/meters in diameter', NULL, '{"IQ":20,"ME":26,"MA":26,"PS":60,"PP":22,"PE":30,"PB":28,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 12000, 4000, 400, NULL, 18, '{"attacks":10,"initiative":6,"strike":4,"dodge":3,"pull":10,"roll":6}', 'Horror/Awe Factor 18 (awe, though evil creatures are horrified). Ten attacks per melee by lasers, physical attacks or psionics, or three by magic. Cannot parry. The block prints "+10 to pull punch, +6 to roll with impact and pull punch"; +10 is stored for pull. Critical strike on a 17-20. +2 to save vs psionic attack, +6 to save vs magic (all); immune to Horror Factor; impervious to possession, illusions and all forms of mind control. All in addition to attribute bonuses. Strength and endurance are supernatural. Spd 44 is on the ground; flying, its natural state, is 126 (approximately 85 mph/136 km), and it swims as fast as it flies.', '[{"name":"Holistic Medicine","pct":98},{"name":"Basic & Advanced Math","pct":98},{"name":"Corroboree","pct":98}]', 'R.C.C. Skills of Note as printed: Holistic Medicine, Basic & Advanced Math, Corroboree, all Navigation skills, all Wilderness skills and all Lore skills at 98%. Understands and speaks all languages at 98% but cannot read.', 'Heals 2D6x100 M.D.C. a minute. Sees 20 miles (32 km) by day or night, plus the invisible and every spectrum of light. Flies at any height, even into space; needs no air and survives any depth. Limited Invulnerability: drugs, poison, disease, heat, cold, lightning, storms and anything airborne do nothing, nor do weapons of Millennium wood or coral. Being made of light, it takes no damage at all from ordinary physical attacks and explosives, S.D.C. or M.D., and a tenth from energy blasts; lasers and radiation pass through harmlessly. Magic, psionics and magic weapons do normal damage, and rune weapons double. Ley Line Drifting, Phasing and Transmission as a Ley Line Walker, at 15th level. Sees through every illusion and dispels it with a flick of the tongue. Control Weather: once per visit it calls gentle heavy rain for about 24 hours over as much as 600 square miles (1554 square km). Resurrection: once per visit it raises 2D6 allies of light who were slain fighting evil within the past 72 hours.', 'All air and water magic and may use all Crystal Magic powers and spells. 4000 P.P.E.; spells cast equal to a 10th level spell caster.', 'All Sensitive powers, plus the Super-Psionic powers of Empathic Transmission, Mind Bolt, Mind Bond and P.P.E. Shield. 400 I.S.P.; equal to a 15th level Mind Melter and a Master Psionic (needs a 10 or higher to save vs psionic attack).', NULL, 'None; they would not work on this creature of light', NULL, 'Does not need or want any', 'A guardian that appears only when something of titanic supernatural scale threatens Australia or mankind, never to meddle in human affairs. It stays just long enough to consume the worst of the evil and leave people hopeful, and each sending costs the distant god some of its own life energy.', 'All Aborigines, all good creatures, all animals and goodly spirits, and Millennium creatures', 'Demons, supernatural evil and evil of all kinds; the darkest and most powerful forces of evil and chaos, Tikilik among them', 'The true Rainbow Serpent, who cut the rivers and called the rain when the world was made, left long ago and is now dimensions away; no statistics are given for the god itself. This is the fragment it sometimes sends: a rainbow that turns snake and slides down from the sky, a mile of translucent colored light gliding a little under 100 feet (30.5 m) above the ground. Since the Rifts came it has appeared three times - to stop Australia being destroyed, to shut a dimensional Rift, and to fight Tikilik. When it goes it leaves a hollow like a river bed. Habitat: the endless Megaverse.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.190-191');
